<title>INDIA: Indian soybean prices steady in central markets.</title>
<headline>Indian soybean prices steady in central markets.</headline>
<dateline>INDORE, India 1996-10-10</dateline>
<text>
<p>Indian soybean prices were steady in central markets on Thursday, dealers said.</p>
<p>They said there was moisture of 10 to 14 percent in new season crops. Soyoil refined fell by 300 rupees per tonne on increased selling from refineries. Soyoil solvent was steady and undertone was weak.</p>
<p>Soymeal and rapeseed extraction prices were steady in thin trade on limited demand. Soymeal yellow was $280 per tonne October delivery and $276 for November, December and January delivery. Rapeseed extraction was $125 per tonne in export.</p>
<p>Rapeseed extraction was 4,200 rupees FOR Bedibunder and was 4,150-4,175 rupees FOR Bhavnagar.</p>
